+---
+title: Adding a built-in ParamType (click.Duration)
+author: HarzerHeribert
+date: 2026-10-15
+cost: { minutes: 2, tokens: 52244 }
+touches:
+  - CHANGES.md
+  - docs/api.md
+  - docs/parameter-types.md
+  - src/click/__init__.py
+  - src/click/types.py
+  - tests/test_types.py
+---
+
+## Decided
+- New built-in types go in src/click/types.py next to their closest sibling (Duration sits after DateTime), with `name` set (drives the default metavar, e.g. DURATION) and a `__repr__` like the others.
+- Wire-up checklist: export in src/click/__init__.py, `autoclass` in docs/api.md and docs/parameter-types.md, tests in tests/test_types.py, entry in CHANGES.md (no Unreleased section existed after 8.5.0, so one was added for 8.6.0).
+- Duration parses with one `re.fullmatch` pattern `(N d)?(N h)?(N m)?(N s)?` (IGNORECASE, `[0-9]` not `\d`); a bare ASCII-digit string means seconds. Non-str, non-timedelta input fails rather than being coerced.
+
+## Tried and ruled out
+- `\d` / `str.isdigit()` alone: they accept non-ASCII digits like full-width "１２"; use `[0-9]` and `isascii()`.
+- `re.match` with `$`: `$` matches before a trailing newline, so "1h\n" would pass; use `fullmatch`.
+
+## Watch out
+- `timedelta(days=huge)` raises OverflowError; catch it and route through `self.fail` so users get a BadParameter, not a traceback.
+- pytest addopts deselects `stress` tests (~31k "deselected" in the summary is normal).
+- ruff isn't installed in the bench venv; format to 88 columns by hand.
+- Pyright flags test_types.py:85 (float_range test) — it was already there, not a regression.
